0:{"buildId":"Nd1cQcP5Lh31_JTWc3jWW","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"post":{"slug":"beginner-cardio-at-home","category":"HOME CARDIO","title":"Beginner cardio workouts you can do at home","description":"Start cardio at home with low-impact movement, simple intervals and beginner-friendly progressions that do not require machines.","lead":"Home cardio can begin with simple movement and a pace you can repeat consistently.","keywords":["cardio workout at home","beginner cardio workout","home cardio","low impact cardio"],"stage":10,"activity":"run","takeaway":"Build the habit and your work capacity before chasing harder intervals.","sections":[{"heading":"Begin with low-impact movement","body":"Marching, step patterns and brisk walking can raise your activity level without requiring jumping. Choose movements that feel stable and give you room to control your breathing."},{"heading":"Use simple work and recovery intervals","body":"Short periods of faster movement followed by easier movement can make pacing clear. Keep the first sessions comfortable enough that you could repeat them later in the week."},{"heading":"Progress duration before complexity","body":"Adding a few minutes is often more useful than constantly changing exercises. Once the session length feels comfortable, you can gradually increase pace or use more demanding movement options."},{"heading":"Pair cardio with strength","body":"Cardio and strength support different parts of general fitness. A balanced week can include both, with easier days between the sessions that challenge you most."}]},"index":9,"total":14,"prevHref":"/blog/strength-and-cardio-same-week","nextHref":"/blog/morning-mobility-routine"}],[["$","script","script-0",{"src":"/_next/static/chunks/1f3e3iqq5mikc.js","async":true}]],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","$4",null,{"name":"Next.MetadataOutlet","children":"$@5"}]}]]}],"isPartial":"$@6","staleTime":"$7","varyParams":null},{"rsc":["$","$1","h",{"children":[nul